# barter-ai schema sync (shared Postgres)

**swaphaven-api owns the database.** barter-ai (`../barter-ai`) shares the same Postgres but keeps a **read-only TypeScript snapshot** at `../barter-ai/src/db/schema/`.

## Automatic local sync (already wired)

These run without manual `cp`:

| Trigger | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Cursor / agent edits `src/db/schema/*.ts` | `.cursor/hooks.json` → `afterFileEdit` → `scripts/sync-barter-ai-schema.mjs` |
| `npm run db:generate` | runs `schema:sync-barter-ai` after drizzle-kit |
| Git commit with staged schema files | `.githooks/pre-commit` (enable once: `npm run setup:git-hooks`) |

Manual fallback: `npm run schema:sync-barter-ai`

## When this rule applies

Any change under `src/db/schema/`, `drizzle/`, or `drizzle.config.ts`.

## Required follow-up (same task / PR)

1. **Migrate here only** — commit `drizzle/*.sql` + `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`; never add migrations to barter-ai.
2. **Confirm sync ran** — check `../barter-ai/src/db/schema/` matches; re-run `npm run schema:sync-barter-ai` if needed.
3. **Verify barter-ai** when present: `cd ../barter-ai && npm run typecheck`
4. **Commit barter-ai** schema changes in the barter-ai repo.

## Do not

- Copy `drizzle/*.sql` or run `db:push` / `migrate` in barter-ai.
- Edit barter-ai schema without matching changes here first.

## One-time git hook setup (manual edits outside Cursor)

```bash
npm run setup:git-hooks
```
